          "metric_value": "3",
          "unit": "$million",
          "source_quote": "ThirdAI Automation, a San Francisco, CA–based causal AI platform for semiconductor manufacturing, has raised $3 million in a Seed round.\nInvestors\nThe round was co-led by Endiya Partners and Capria Ventures.\nEndiya Partners is an early-stage venture capital (VC) firm headquartered in Hyderabad, Telangana, India, that invests in and helps scale technology-focused startups with regional and global ambitions. Founded in 2015, the firm focuses on deep tech, healthcare, and enterprise SaaS.\nCapria Ventures is a Seattle-based venture capital firm specializing in the Global South, including India, Southeast Asia, Africa, and Latin America. Managing over $188 million in assets, the firm focuses on tech-enabled startups and founders driving digital transformation and scalable impact in emerging markets.\nThirdAI Automation Use of Funds\nThe funding will accelerate product development, expand engineering capabilities, strengthen its go-to-market strategy, and scale global deployments of its causal AI platform for semiconductor and other industrial manufacturing sectors.\nAbout ThirdAI Automation\n",
